## How to Run (After Changes)

```bash
# Step 1: Retrain the MLP (will take longer with physics losses)
python trajectory_prediction/train_mlp.py

# Step 2: Predict trajectory for a peptide
python trajectory_prediction/predict_trajectory.py --peptide AC

# Step 3: Visualize it
python scripts/visualization.py --peptide AC --source predicted --frame 50
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> You **must retrain** the model from scratch after these changes. The old `trajectory_mlp.pt` checkpoint won't work because the architecture is different (residual connection).

